# Backend

## Structure

- Routes: `backend/app/api/` (`articles`, `clusters`, `bias`, `rumors`, **`ingest`**, **`admin`**, **`verify`**, **`verifications`**) mounted in `app/api/__init__.py`
- Models: `app/models/` (`article`, `cluster`, `source`, **`verified_claim`**); Pydantic: `app/schemas/` (`ingest.py`, **`admin.py`**, **`verify.py`**, **`verification.py`**)
- Business logic: `app/services/` — `rss_parser`, **`rss_ingestion`**, `ai_client`, **`admin_stats`**, **`admin_sources`**, **`ops_alerts`**, **`verification_*`** (submit, runner, pipeline, jobs, job_stream, fetch, slug), **`semantic_cache`**, **`embeddings`**, **`ai_guardrails`**, **`ai_input_sanitizer`**, **`object_storage`**, **`ingest_queue`**, **`db_extensions`** — keep route handlers thin
- Workers: `app/workers/` — `celery_app`, `ingest_tasks`, verification tasks; queues `ingest` + `verification`
- Monitoring: `app/core/sentry_init.py` — call `init_sentry()` from `main.py` (not inside lifespan)
- Rate limits: `app/core/rate_limit.py`, `app/middleware/rate_limit_middleware.py` — Redis when `REDIS_URL` set; tiered limits for verify (anon/auth/Pro JWT), ingest, admin
- Seed data: `app/data/bd_sources_seed.py`
- Config: `app/core/config.py` (`Settings`, prefix `/api/v1`, `ingest_api_key`, `admin_api_key`, pool modes, `redis_url`, `ingest_async_enabled`, rate limits, semantic cache, optional `sentry_*`, `healthchecks_*`, `telegram_*`, object storage)
- DB: `app/core/database.py` (`SessionLocal`, `get_db`); ORM `create_all` + **`apply_sql_migrations`** (`backend/migrations/*.sql` — `001_verified_claims_pgvector_fts.sql`, **`002_sources_disabled.sql`**) in `app/main.py` lifespan
- CLI: `backend/scripts/ingest_rss.py` (`npm run ingest:backend`); optional `backend/scripts/verification_worker.py` for local verification queue debugging
- Health: `GET /health` (outside API prefix)
- Local stack: `docker-compose.yml` — Postgres pgvector, Redis, API, worker

## API surface

- `GET /api/v1/articles`, `/clusters`, `/clusters/{slug}`, `/bias`, `/rumors`
- **`GET /api/v1/admin/overview`**, **`POST /api/v1/admin/sources`**, **`DELETE /api/v1/admin/sources/{id}`** — `X-Admin-Key` when `ADMIN_API_KEY` is set; overview lists all sources with **`disabled`** flag; DELETE **soft-disables** seed sources or any source with articles (hard-deletes only empty custom sources); POST re-enables when the same name was disabled
- **`POST /api/v1/ingest`** — Celery (`ingest` queue) when `REDIS_URL` + `INGEST_ASYNC_ENABLED`; else inline; **202** + `job_id` when queued; **`GET /api/v1/ingest/jobs/{job_id}`**; `X-Ingest-Key` when `INGEST_API_KEY` is set
- **`POST /api/v1/verify`** — guardrailed user submit (`VerifyResponse`; may return cache hit, blocked guardrail, or `job_id`)
- **`POST /api/v1/verifications`** — create with semantic cache; **`GET /jobs/{job_id}`**, **`GET /jobs/{job_id}/events`** (SSE), **`WebSocket /jobs/{job_id}/ws`**
- **`GET /api/v1/verifications`**, **`GET /verifications/search?q=`**, **`GET /verifications/{slug}`** (completed claims only)
- OpenAPI: `/docs` when server is running

## RSS ingestion

- Entry point: `run_rss_ingest(session)` in `app/services/rss_ingestion.py`
- Seeds/updates `Source` rows from `BD_SOURCE_SEED` (does not overwrite feed URL/bias on **disabled** rows), fetches only **non-disabled** sources via `fetch_feed_items`, skips duplicate URLs, assigns articles to existing clusters by title similarity or creates new `Cluster` with unique slug
- May call `ai_client.summarize_cluster` when a cluster gains multiple articles
- Returns `IngestResult` counts + per-source error strings (ingest continues on fetch failures)

## Verification

- Prefer **`submit_verify_request`** for `/verify`; **`create_verification`** + job watchers for `/verifications`
- Persist rows in `VerifiedClaim`; embeddings via raw SQL (`embedding` vector column); full-text `search_vector` for `/search`
- Celery task when broker available; else `BackgroundTasks` + `execute_verification_job`
- Input: always through **`ai_input_sanitizer`** + **`ai_guardrails`** (`assess_user_content` — injection/heuristic blocks before LLM); respect rate limits on verify routes

## Patterns

- Use **async** endpoints and DB/HTTP for I/O-bound work
- Add new resources as a router module + schema + model; register on `api_router`
- AI calls go through `AIClient`; respect `settings.ai_provider` and optional API keys
- Scheduled ingest: cron/worker should call CLI or `POST /api/v1/ingest` so Healthchecks/Telegram hooks run
- `ops_alerts.notify_payment_webhook` — stub for future bKash webhook handlers
- New SQL that ORM cannot express: add idempotent file under `backend/migrations/` and run via `db_extensions`

